.TH RT_SIGQUEUEINFO 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
rt_sigqueueinfo \- sends a signal using the raw linux rt_sigqueueinfo syscall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <signal.h>
.B int rt_sigqueueinfo(pid_t process, int signal, const siginfo_t* information);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a signal using the raw Linux rt_sigqueueinfo syscall. information uses the kernel layout and must satisfy Linux si_code and permission rules; queued data is in data.queued.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rt_sigqueueinfo (2)
